470 - There's Sunshine in My Soul Today
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 470
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[D]There’s [G]sunshine in my soul today,
[G]More glorious [D/F#]and bright
[G/D]Than glows in any earthly sky,
[G]For Jesus [F#dim]is my [Am]light.

Refrain:
[Am]O there's [D/A]sunshine, blessed [G]sunshine,
[C]When the peaceful, [G]happy moments [Am]roll
[D7/A]When Jesus [C/G]shows [G]His [C]smiling face
[G]There is sunshine [F#dim]in the [G]soul.

Verse 2:
[D]There's [G]music in my soul today,
[G]A carol [F#dim]to [D/F#]my King,
[G/D]And Jesus, listening, can hear
[G]The songs [F#dim]I cannot [Am]sing.

Verse 3:
[D]There's [G]springtime in my soul today,
[G]For when the [F#dim]Lord [D/F#]is near,
[G/D]The dove of peace sings in my heart,
[G]The flowers [F#dim]of grace appear.

Verse 4:
[D]Theres [G]gladness in my soul today,
[G]And hope, and [F#dim]praise, [D/F#]and love,
[G/D]For blessings which He gives me now,
[G]For joys [F#dim]"laid up" above.
